    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="1259" n="1243" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg1243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 55D128: Black Book, Tab 29: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United Nations Command</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ridgway</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Advance
                        Headquarters, United Nations Command, Korea</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-05T10:52:00+09:00">5 December
                            1951—10:52 a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>CX–58695. Desired that UNC initial position under agenda item 5 be phrased as
                    follows:</p>
                <p>“Each side agrees to recommend to its respective governmental authorities that
                    they give consideration to the convening of a conference of the political
                    representatives of both sides to discuss appropriate matters arising from but
                    not resolved by the armistice agreement”.</p>
            </div>
